SYNOPSIS:
              Here's a version of Space Empire for MAXS BBS boards only!
              It takes the Paragon compatible version of Space Empire
              that runs on MAXS and solves all its little bugs 'n' features,
              such as non working msg functions, snipers, crashing 'n' 
              locking etc.  Apart from that it's not much different...


COMPATIBILITY:
              This door was developed on a WB2.04 A3000/040, and tested on a
              WB2.04 A500.  Someone wanna' test it on a WB1.3 machine?


INSTALLATION:
              Like all my other doors, t'is vewee, vewee, thimple... 

eg:  KEY  FUNCTION  EXTRAS  LOW  HIGH   PATH/FILENAME
      S      34       0     10   10000  DOORS:SE/Ari_SE SE/

              The PATH/FILENAME contains the normal stuff to find the door,
              plus the argument "SE/", so that the door can find
              all of its config and data files.  Don't use the FULL path as
              the argument, (ie "DOORS:SE/" will NOT work), as the main DOORS
              path is grabbed from "MAXsBBS.config".

      *NOTE*  You can name the directory/path anything you want, but it
              must be short enough so that it and the argument fit!  If this
              doesn't make sense then don't worry, you'll get it after a
              while >-]

      *NOTE*  You must have the "/" after the argument path, otherwise this
              door won't run! 


CONFIGURATION:
              There SHOULD be 5 files, ALL have to be named exactly as
              shown, otherwise NO Space Empire!

              	Ari_SE                     ;Space Empire executable.
                SpcEmp.CFG                 ;Space Empire config file.
                SpcEmp.doc                 ;Space Empire documentation.
                SpcEmp.help                ;Space EMpire Help file.
                SEHigh_Scores.text         ;Space Empire High Scores.

              Upon initial start-up, two #?.DAT files will be created by the
              door.  

                SpcPlayer.DAT              ;Current Game's Players data file.
                Teams.DAT                  ;Current Game's Teams data file.

              During gameplay two #?.txt files will be created by the door 
              
                news.txt                   ;Current Game's News file.                
                scores.txt                 ;Current Game's Scores file.

              Editable files.
  
                SpcEmp.CFG          ;Contains two entries, paths to where the
                                     news and scores files are to be created.

                                     eg: DOORS:SE1/news.txt
                                         DOORS:SE1/scores.txt


                SEHigh_Scores.text  ;Sysop must add each winner of each game
                                     manually.  I MIGHT make it automatic in
                                     a future version, if anyone asks?

              Each time a game is finished, the Sysop must delete the two 
              #?.DAT files, and Space Empire will reset itself!


TECHNICAL:    
              I grabbed the original Paragon source and spent about a week
              cleaning it up, removing bugs, and adding a few extra features.
              All of it re-compiled under SAS C 6.3


